{
 "title": "Phase-fit condition for the hold-fix NIS limit on --preset urban",
 "doc": "docs/rtk_hold_fix_phase_fit.md",
 "reference_use": "The reference trajectory and the truth-DD export are used only for scoring, for the analysis-only phase audit and for the motivation analysis; nothing here is a solver input.",
 "frozen_rule": "Frozen 2026-10-28 before the replay. Branch claude/confident-clarke-k37g2b on develop 3cb7230 (#671).\nChange: opt-in RTKConfig::hold_fix_update_nis_max_phase_fit (CLI --hold-fix-update-nis-max-phase-fit, default 0 = off).\nWith hold_fix_max_update_nis_per_observation set, the hold_fix_update_nis rejection applies only when the\ninteger-free DD carrier-phase fit of the hold position (mean over the hold pairs of cos(2*pi*r/lambda), its\nmaximum on a +-0.10 m / 0.02 m grid around the hold position) is below the value, or unknown (< 10 usable pairs).\nRecipes: U = --preset urban; UH = U --hold-fix-max-update-nis-per-obs 10;\nUHP = UH --hold-fix-update-nis-max-phase-fit 0.5.\nThresholds are not tuned here: 10 is the NIS value of #663, 0.5 / 10 pairs / +-0.10 m are AF_INCONSISTENT,\nMIN_DD and NEIGHBOURHOOD of scripts/analysis/truth_dd/phase_audit.py.\nDisclosure: the AND of NIS and phase misfit was chosen after seeing, on these same ten runs under U, the per-hold\ndistributions of NIS and of AFn at the solver position (truth-DD export, elevation >= 15 deg, no LLI).\nGates (as #663): A (more FIX and no more wrong FIX than RTKLIB, audited labels), W (wrong FIX >0.5 m not\nincreased vs U on any run), L (U-correct FIX lost <= 1% on every run), M (missing epochs and Hp95 not increased).\nPrediction from the direct effect on U holds: genuine wrong hold fixes 183 -> about 80; U-correct holds rejected\n<= 0.4% of a run's correct FIX before knock-on effects; nagoya/run3 loss < 1% (UH: 9.90%).\nFlag off: U POS byte-identical to the develop binary on all ten runs.\n",
 "frozen_rule_sha256": "d3387e3e8e03c157ec15cf15f61dfcaa9af59beb72da4d700e65cc3ed0ec2dce",
 "frozen_rule_variant": "Frozen 2026-10-28 after the UHP replay (frozen_rule_uhp.txt, sha256 d3387e3e...) and before this replay.\nBinary as UHP (bin_uhp/gnss_solve sha256 56b7f8c8...). UHP2 = UHP + --hold-fix-update-nis-keeps-hold-run (#663 option, unchanged).\nReason, seen on the UHP replay: on nagoya/run3 the 98 lost U-correct epochs follow one correct rejection (553961.2,\nU hold 0.87 m off, phase fit 0.37) that made the epoch FLOAT and closed the hold path; U's later holds were correct.\nGates unchanged (A, W, L <= 1%, M). Prediction: nagoya/run3 loss falls below UHP's 9.32%; the Tokyo PPC losses,\nmostly later AR failures (lambda_not_fixed, position_jump), change little; audited wrong FIX stay within +10 of UHP.\n",
 "frozen_rule_variant_sha256": "bbbb16cc19177dac8163b1e5d35b9e7086a862e7ccb81549cace301f0c491c83",
 "binary": {
  "source": "claude/confident-clarke-k37g2b 54127df (develop 3cb7230 + the option)",
  "gnss_solve_sha256": "56b7f8c80ca1c9c9113171a76b60fe82c92cc56b0b156969730c20d37d66c23c",
  "byte_identity": "--preset urban POS byte-identical to the develop 3cb7230 binary on all ten runs (flag off)"
 },
